WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.310
Isabel opened her suitcase and started to unpack.

2
00:00:04.311 --> 00:00:07.252
Her father had already left for a meeting.

3
00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:12.408
"This is going to be so boring," she mumbled.

4
00:00:12.409 --> 00:00:17.457
"How can you have fun when it's dark and cold all the time?"

5
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:20.443
Isabel and her father lived in Florida.

6
00:00:20.444 --> 00:00:26.664
But for the next month, her father was working at a university in Tromsø, Norway.

7
00:00:26.672 --> 00:00:32.642
The city was north of the Arctic Circle, and they had arrived during the polar night.

8
00:00:32.643 --> 00:00:39.096
Because of Earth's tilt, polar regions receive almost no sunlight during this time.

9
00:00:39.097 --> 00:00:45.269
In Tromsø this lasts from November through January—three whole months!

10
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.383
Just then Isabel heard a knock.

11
00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:54.256
It was the university student who lived next door.

12
00:00:54.257 --> 00:00:57.660
"Hello," Erik said with a friendly smile.

13
00:00:57.661 --> 00:01:03.002
"Ready for your tour of Tromsø? Dress warmly—it's cold outside!"

14
00:01:03.003 --> 00:01:12.249
Isabel forced a polite smile in return.

15
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:19.702
"Ugh," she thought. "Right now my friends are probably at the beach!"

16
00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:27.050
Isabel followed Erik as he pointed out restaurants, theaters, and shops.

17
00:01:27.051 --> 00:01:31.393
She spotted a group of kids wearing ski gear.

18
00:01:31.394 --> 00:01:34.228
"Are they going skiing?"

19
00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.090
Erik grinned. "Why does that surprise you?"

20
00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:43.362
"It's dark outside! Isn't it dangerous to ski now?"

21
00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:49.258
"There are lights on the slopes. And it's fun to ski at night!"

22
00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:54.187
"What else can you do during the polar night?" Isabel asked.

23
00:01:54.188 --> 00:01:58.479
"Well, many people go to concerts and cook meals together.

24
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.213
People like to go ice fishing and ice skating.

25
00:02:02.214 --> 00:02:05.173
We can even feed reindeer."

26
00:02:05.174 --> 00:02:11.697
Isabel laughed. "I could never do some of those things in Florida!

27
00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:17.599
But it must be hard to live with so little sunlight for three whole months."

28
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.459
"Some people find it difficult.

29
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:24.558
They use special light boxes that give the effect of the sun.

30
00:02:24.559 --> 00:02:27.217
Other people take vitamin D pills.

31
00:02:27.218 --> 00:02:31.785
Not getting enough sunlight can cause a lack of vitamin D."

32
00:02:31.786 --> 00:02:35.633
Erik shrugged. "I love the polar night."

33
00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.654
"What's summer like?"

34
00:02:37.655 --> 00:02:39.767
"Great," Erik said.

35
00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:42.976
"From May to July, we have the midnight sun.

36
00:02:42.977 --> 00:02:45.675
It stays light all day long.

37
00:02:45.676 --> 00:02:53.181
You can go hiking or swimming in the middle of the night."

38
00:02:53.182 --> 00:02:58.880
They went into a cafe to get warm.

39
00:02:58.881 --> 00:03:03.798
"So, what would you like to do while you're here?" Erik asked.

40
00:03:03.799 --> 00:03:09.144
"Actually . . ." Isabel took a sip of her steaming hot chocolate.

41
00:03:09.145 --> 00:03:12.182
"Everything sounds fun!"

42
00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:17.545
Isabel's month in Tromsø flew by.

43
00:03:17.546 --> 00:03:20.401
She went skiing and ice fishing.

44
00:03:20.402 --> 00:03:23.077
She sledded down snowy hills!

45
00:03:23.078 --> 00:03:30.770
On her last night in Norway, Erik came by.

46
00:03:30.771 --> 00:03:33.796
"I have a surprise," he said.

47
00:03:33.797 --> 00:03:40.375
"We're going to drive outside the city for a show."

48
00:03:40.376 --> 00:03:44.723
Forty minutes later Erik pulled into a parking lot.

49
00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:50.684
They got out of the car and followed a trail to a dark field.

50
00:03:50.685 --> 00:03:54.625
People were standing there, staring up at the sky.

51
00:03:54.626 --> 00:03:58.982
"Whoa!" Isabel gasped.

52
00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:05.277
Waves of green light danced above. "The northern lights!"

53
00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:11.283
Erik grinned. "They're caused by particles from the sun entering Earth's atmosphere.

54
00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:21.361
You can see the show best when you're close to the North Pole."

55
00:04:21.362 --> 00:04:26.959
Soon they were driving back to Tromsø.

56
00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.538
"Ready to return home to warm, sunny Florida?" Erik asked.

57
00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:33.516
Isabel shook her head.

58
00:04:33.517 --> 00:04:45.937
"Nope! I love the polar night. It's beautiful—and fun!"

